    "WAON Number" to R.string.text_2b133418c95162b5,
    "WAON history comes from service 680B. Each record is two 16-byte blocks; bytes 18-28 are MSB-first packed fields." to R.string.text_c2aff412729ed929,
    "WAON history record layout for service `680B` (`0B68` little-endian on card I/O). Bytes `0-12` are the terminal number, `13-14` are the record number, byte `17` is the transaction type, and bytes `18-28` contain MSB-first packed date, balance, usage amount, and charge amount fields." to R.string.text_4e639786fed4f2e3,
    "Wallet stack" to R.string.text_f14334788e02b975,
    "What is shared?" to R.string.text_eaf88324289db8ab,
    "When enabled, KS X 6924 scans probe all SFIs with read-only APDUs and preserve every readable record and short-EF binary block in Raw Data. Scans take longer." to R.string.text_582785219fc2383e,
    "When enabled, eligible T-money and EZL/Cashbee scans upload technical trip records for format analysis. Uploaded fields are a dedup hash of card ID plus raw bytes, a hashed card ID, the last 4 characters of the card ID, bytes 0x05-0x08, bytes 0x09-0x0A, and the full raw bytes. Uploads use HTTPS and you can disable this at any time." to R.string.text_41c3b1fb208c5473,
